\newlabel{fig:fourier}{{3}{5}{\textbf {Circuit Imprint: loss-geometry independently recovers the circuit's dimensionality.} \emph {Left:} Token-embedding Fourier spectrum across training (bright = high amplitude). Through the memorisation phase all frequencies are dim and equal; at the grokking transition a small set abruptly activates (vertical green dashed line) while others remain near zero. \emph {Right:} Active frequency count (orange) and $\hat \lambda _H$ (teal) both transition at the same training step and reach consistent values post-grokking. The two signals are derived from entirely different objects (embedding spectrum vs.\ loss-surface curvature) and share no information, yet converge simultaneously}{figure.caption.3}{}}
